						id="GenericpreviewMobile">Title : FluView : U.S. Influenza Surveillance System : purpose and methods

Corporate Authors(s) : National Center for Immunization and Respiratory Diseases (U.S.). Influenza Division.

Published Date : 08/17/2022

Series : FluView

URL : https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/120452

</textarea>
					<div aria-label="APA Preview" class="form-control citation-preview" style=" display: none; ; white-space: pre-wrap; min-height: 140px;"
						id="APApreviewMobile">National Center for Immunization and Respiratory Diseases (U.S.). Influenza Division. (2022). <i>FluView : U.S. Influenza Surveillance System : purpose and methods</i>. <a href="https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/120452" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/120452</a></div>
					<div aria-label="Chicago Preview" class="form-control citation-preview" style=" display: none; ; white-space: pre-wrap; min-height: 140px;"
						id="chicagopreviewMobile">National Center for Immunization and Respiratory Diseases (U.S.). Influenza Division.. <i>FluView : U.S. Influenza Surveillance System : purpose and methods</i>. 2022. <a href="https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/120452" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/120452</a>.</div>
					<div aria-label="MLA Preview" class="form-control citation-preview" style=" display: none; ; white-space: pre-wrap; min-height: 140px;"
						id="MLApreviewMobile">National Center for Immunization and Respiratory Diseases (U.S.). Influenza Division. <i>FluView : U.S. Influenza Surveillance System : purpose and methods</i>. 2022, Stacks. <a href="https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/120452" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://stacks.cdc.gov/view/cdc/120452</a>.</div>
					<textarea aria-label="RIS Preview" disabled readonly class="form-control" style=" display: none; "
						id="RISpreviewMobile">Export RIS Citation Information.</textarea>
					<textarea hidden class="d-none" id="RIScitation120452">TY  - 
A2  - National Center for Immunization and Respiratory Diseases (U.S.). Influenza Division.
AB  - The Influenza Division at CDC collects, compiles, and analyzes information on influenza activity year-round in the United States. FluView, a weekly influenza surveillance report, and FluView Interactive, an online application which allows for more in-depth exploration of influenza surveillance data, are updated each week. The data presented each week are preliminary and may change as more data are received.
AB  - U.S. World Health Organization (WHO) Collaborating Laboratories System and the National Respiratory and Enteric Virus Surveillance System (NREVSS) -- Virus Characterization -- Surveillance for Novel Influenza A Viruses -- U.S. Outpatient Influenza-like Illness Surveillance Network (ILINet) -- ILI Activity Indicator Map -- Long-term Care Facilities -- FluSurv-NET -- HHS Protect Hospitalization Surveillance -- National Center for Health Statistics (NCHS) Mortality Surveillance Data -- Influenza-Associated Pediatric Mortality Surveillance System -- Summary of the Geographic Spread of Influenza.
AN  - cdc:120452
CY  - Atlanta, GA
KW  - Computer Systems
KW  - Data Collection
KW  - Datasets as Topic
